        "original_id": "83f60eba-6aeb-549d-9685-ea50166f4988",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lindsey Islands, Canisteo Peninsula, Amundsen Sea, Indiana\n- People: Alton A. Lindsey\n- Organizations: Purdue University\n- Roles: ecologist, professor of forest ecology\n- Concepts: nature preserves\n\nFacts:\n- Lindsey Islands is a group of islands located just off the northwest tip of Canisteo Peninsula in the Amundsen Sea.\n- Alton A. Lindsey was born on May 7, 1907, and died on December 19, 1999.\n- Alton A. Lindsey was a pioneering ecologist.\n- From 1947 to 1973, Alton A. Lindsey was a professor of forest ecology at Purdue University in Indiana.\n- Alton A. Lindsey was largely responsible for the creation of nature preserves in Indiana.",
